1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Nine to nine. Six days a week. In China, it has a name: 996.

2
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:11,300
That's 72 hours a week — almost two full-time jobs in one.

3
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:18,100
For years, the quiet rule at many tech firms: work hard, or someone else will.

4
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:26,800
In 2021, China's top court called a 72-hour week illegal — overtime caps near 36 hours a month.

5
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:34,200
One delivery driver, fired for refusing 996, sued — and won about $1,100.

6
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:38,700
So: the paycheck, or the hours back? Tell me below.
